  "id": "COMPOUND:20825 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between 7,2'-Dihydroxy-4',5'-methylenedioxyisoflavan and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, as this compound is identified as a target of multiple downstream molecules that ultimately interact with the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2) subunit EZH2. The compound acts as a common target for several structurally diverse compounds, all of which are implicated in the regulation of gene expression through the PRC2 complex. This indicates that the compound may exert its biological effects by modulating the activity of the PRC2 complex, potentially through direct or indirect interactions with EZH2. The consistent targeting of the compound to the PRC2 complex across different pathways supports the hypothesis that it may function as a PRC2 inhibitor, thereby influencing gene regulation. The evidence is robust and consistent, with multiple independent pathways converging on the same target, reinforcing the likelihood of a mechanistic relationship.",
